{
  "_howTo": [
    "Operation entries select provider, model, effort and fallback together (operations, operations.X:taskType or taskTypes). For fix and ci-heal, codex.modelByTask overlays model, effort and retry through standard policy → platform → settings → env.",
    "An entry with inherit:true preserves the existing evidence/tier router. taskTypes entries override inherited operations; operations may also use operation:taskType keys (review-seat:security, for example).",
    "Aliases below resolve to explicit model IDs. Every policy-routed dispatch requires the critical-work check; criticalWorkGate.kinds also governs inherited routing. A closed gate takes the Claude fallback.",
    "Fallbacks are tried in order for unavailable providers or definite pre-launch refusals. Fix/heal Codex task retry settings replace the same-provider retry rungs before the Claude fallback. Never retry an indeterminate or already-started launch. Invalid edits retain the last good policy and log the validation error.",
    "Card 84 (retired 2026-10-22, operator): review-pr mandatory seats are plain Claude again — an open-ended shadow brings no value; agy-claude may later replace Claude as a reviewer only as a direct replacement with a promotion rule. The advisory agy-correctness seat is removed. agy-claude (opus-5-5) is a fallback on the Claude-only rows (fix:ruling-escalation-stronger, and after claude on build).",
    "Review operation judges use judge:<operation> (for example judge:review-pr); review-seat:<lens> selects an added seat. Native agent-only adapters take the first Claude entry; unsupported or missing adapters take the declared fallback. Existing CLI pins remain explicit per-run choices.",
    "Astra effort correctness is unproven (see CODEX_TIER_EFFORT in we:scripts/lib/codex-model-routing.mjs): effort is a cost/latency dial until measured.",
    "Operator 2026-09-30: Gemini only with confidence of value. smallPrepare controls the <=3, explicitly well-scoped, no-design prepare exception; widen it here as evidence arrives. Unknown size/design stays Codex.",
    "Operator 2026-10-15: Claude workers default to Sonnet to contain cost. Fix rounds and send-backs alone never justify Opus; only a critical-work verdict may raise a Claude fix to Opus. Overlay dispatch smoke pins the cheapest Claude alias (haiku, else sonnet)."
  ],
